TLS certificate for this server

The installer creates a self-signed certificate here:
  sentora.crt         certificate plus any intermediate certificates (public)
  sentora-chain.crt   intermediate certificates only, for ProFTPD (public)
  sentora.key         private key (root only)

Apache (the panel and webmail), Postfix (ports 25, 465, 587), Dovecot (IMAP,
POP3, ManageSieve) and ProFTPD (FTPS) all use these files.

Let's Encrypt through Sencrypt: once you issue a certificate for the panel
domain in Sencrypt, the daemon copies it here within 5 minutes, after every
renewal too, and reloads Postfix, Dovecot and ProFTPD. Apache uses the Sencrypt
files directly. The self-signed pair is kept as selfsigned.crt/selfsigned.key.

To use a certificate from somewhere else (your own company CA), replace the
three files, keep the names, then run:
  chmod 600 sentora.key
  systemctl reload apache2 postfix dovecot proftpd
